Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: reuse a large enough allocation

Variant of candidate.patch that additionally restores the reuse the
pinned fast path evidently intended: a request no larger than the
existing allocation keeps it.

This is NOT behaviour preserving.  Because the pinned condition is
inverted, reuse has never occurred, so every caller has so far received
a freshly allocated buffer.  Adopting this variant requires evidence
that each of the repeat-call sites writes every byte the firmware reads
before submission.  See AUDIT.md: that evidence does not exist offline
for the per-frame scratch paths.

Signed-off-by: tankbottoms <tankbottoms@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c
@@ -73,18 +73,22 @@
 
 int avd_buf_alloc(struct avd_dev *avd, struct avd_buf *buf, size_t size)
 {
-	if (!buf->cpu && size < buf->size)
+	if (buf->cpu && size <= buf->size)
 		return 0;
 	else if (buf->cpu)
 		avd_buf_free(avd, buf);
 
 	if (size <= 0)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+
+	buf->cpu = dma_alloc_coherent(avd->dev, size, &buf->addr, GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!buf->cpu) {
+		memset(buf, 0, sizeof(*buf));
 		return -ENOMEM;
+	}
 
 	buf->size = size;
-	buf->cpu =
-		dma_alloc_coherent(avd->dev, buf->size, &buf->addr, GFP_KERNEL);
-	return buf->cpu ? 0 : -ENOMEM;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 void avd_buf_free(struct avd_dev *avd, struct avd_buf *buf)
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-h264.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-h264.c
